<title>ESTONIA: ESTONIA - HOIU ORDERS RATING FROM MOODY'S.</title>
<headline>ESTONIA - HOIU ORDERS RATING FROM MOODY'S.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hoiupank, the third largest bank in Estonia, said on Monday it had ordered a credit rating from Moody's.</p>
<p>&quot;We hope the estimate for Hoiupank and Estonia will be investment grade,&quot; Heino Viik, the director of the bank's finance division, told Reuters.</p>
<p>Hoiupank decided on Moody's because Estonia's central bank will also order a country rating from the agency, Viik said.</p>
<p>He said the bank does not know when the rating will be ready, before or after the rating for the country.</p>
<p>Estonia's central bank said earlier that it planned to order a credit rating for the country and that Moody's is the most likely candidate.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
